.TH RESOLVER 5
.SH NAME
resolver \- resolver configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
/etc/resolv.conf is optional. Lines specify domain followed by a default
domain, search followed by up to six domains, or nameserver followed by an
IPv4 address. Up to three nameservers are retained. Blank lines, # and ;
comments, invalid addresses and lines longer than 1023 bytes are ignored.
Later domain or search directives replace the earlier choice.
.PP
LOCALDOMAIN overrides the configured domain/search with its first word,
following 4.4BSD-Lite2. Without a domain, use the suffix of the full hostname.
The derived search list contains up to three levels, stopping at two domain
components. With no server configured, query 127.0.0.1 port 53.
The defaults are five seconds and four attempts with exponential backoff.
The state in _res and its search strings is not reentrant.
